Installing git-dupe

Git runs git-dupe for `git dupe ...` when the executable git-dupe stands in a
directory on PATH. Its manual page, git-dupe.1, is shown by `man git-dupe`, and
by `git dupe --help` while Git's help format is man, its default, when it
stands in the man1 directory of a manual path. Installing is those two copies,
into directories the first line makes where they are missing. From the
directory that holds this note, with ~/.local/bin on PATH and ~/.local/share/man
on the manual path, run:

    $ mkdir -p ~/.local/bin ~/.local/share/man/man1
    $ cp git-dupe ~/.local/bin/
    $ cp git-dupe.1 ~/.local/share/man/man1/

Any other directory on PATH, and the man1 directory of any other manual path,
serve the same. `git dupe help` needs the executable alone.
